invariant: INV-16
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-trust-separation.sh
reason: the Makefile stops refusing the X25519 variable, so a build that
  still passes X25519=wide gets the 16-word field with no word said, where
  its builder expects the wide one. lint-trust-separation's refused rows
  require make print-lib-def to fail for X25519=wide and X25519=portable,
  on a device object and on a host object.

--- old
ifneq ($(origin X25519),undefined)
--- new
ifneq (,)
